        "original_id": "d1bd9f0b-a3f9-5232-9288-c2f0a52016fd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lukas Rossi, Terry Kath, Ben Moody, Miles McPherson, Josh Newell\n- Bands and Projects: Rock Star Supernova, Chicago, The Halo Method, We Are the Fallen, Evanescence, Daylight Division, In This Moment\n- Roles: rock musician, guitarist, drummer, vocalist, bassist, songwriter, lead singer, founding member\n- Media and Topics: CBS Television reality series, televised audition contest, hard rock supergroup\n\nFacts:\n- Terry Alan Kath was born on January 31, 1946, and he became an American musician and songwriter.\n- Terry Kath was the original guitarist, one of the lead singers, and a founding member of the rock band Chicago.\n- Terry Kath died on January 23, 1978.\n- Lukas Rossi was born on December 21, 1976, and he is a Canadian rock musician.\n- Lukas Rossi won a CBS Television reality series that was a televised audition contest to become the lead singer of the hard rock supergroup Rock Star Supernova.\n- The Halo Method consisted of guitarist Ben Moody, drummer Miles McPherson, vocalist Lukas Rossi, and bassist Josh Newell.\n- Ben Moody was associated with We Are the Fallen and was formerly a member of Evanescence.\n- Lukas Rossi was formerly associated with Rock Star Supernova and Daylight Division.\n- Josh Newell was formerly a member of In This Moment.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
